{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["The meaning of <b>And after the sixty-two weeks, an anointed one shall be cut off</b> — that there shall not be over Israel a king from among them, and <b>the city and the sanctuary</b> a coming <b>prince's people</b> shall destroy — he is Vespasian, commander of the king of Rome, when he came upon Jerusalem with his son. Concerning them too it is written in the fourth vision: <b>And arms from him shall stand and profane the sanctuary, the fortress</b>, <b>and they removed the daily offering.</b>" "And the sense of <b>and his end shall come</b> — his end shall come by ships." "<b>And until the end, war</b> — that he waged war for many years against Jerusalem, until it was ruined, desolate."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's lemma quotes the verse with the words 'the city and the sanctuary' appearing in the middle of v. 26, reflecting the full verse sequence rather than strict word order."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:43.592270943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}